{"segments": [
 {"id": "hero-01", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "Relative pronouns. The one who, the thing which.", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "hero-02", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "In English we say: the student who passed.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["sub"]},
 {"id": "hero-03", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "Here, the little word, who, joins the noun to a short clause about it. It is a relative pronoun.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": []},
 {"id": "hero-04", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "In Arabic, a relative pronoun is fixed. Its ending does not change. The only exception is a pair of words for two. They come in chapter six.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": []},
 {"id": "hero-05", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "And it never stands alone. A clause always comes after it.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-title-01", "scene": "c01-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter one. The table to learn.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-01", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "Here are the relatives to learn by heart.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-table-02", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The first one is for one male, or one masculine thing.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["row:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-03", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِي", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-04", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The student who passed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-table-05", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-06", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The second one is for one female, or one feminine thing.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["row:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-07", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّتِي", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-08", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The girl who passed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-table-09", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الْبِنْتُ الَّتِي نَجَحَتْ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:3"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-10", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The third one is for a group of males.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["row:3"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-11", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:4"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-12", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The students who passed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-table-13", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "الطُّلَّابُ الَّذِينَ نَجَحُوا", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:5"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-14", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The last row is for a group of females. It has two words, and both are correct.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["row:4"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-15", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّاتِي", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["ar:6"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-16", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّوَاتِي", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:7"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-17", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "The women who passed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-table-18", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "ar", "text": "النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي نَجَحْنَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:8"]},
 {"id": "c01-table-19", "scene": "c01-table", "lang": "en", "text": "In every example, the relative comes right after the noun.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-cols-01", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "en", "text": "Next, two relatives that are general. No noun comes before them.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-cols-02", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "en", "text": "The first means the one who. It is for people.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["col:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-cols-03", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "ar", "text": "مَنْ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c01-cols-04", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "en", "text": "The one who passed came.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-cols-05", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "ar", "text": "جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-cols-06", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "en", "text": "The second means what. It is for things.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["col:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-cols-07", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "ar", "text": "مَا", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-cols-08", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "en", "text": "I read what the teacher wrote.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-cols-09", "scene": "c01-cols", "lang": "ar", "text": "قَرَأْتُ مَا كَتَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ", "pause": 0.7, "cues": ["ar:3"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-01", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "en", "text": "A tip on spelling. These three are written with a single L, with a shadda on it.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["show"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-02", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِي", "pause": 0.35, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-03", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّتِي", "pause": 0.35, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-04", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-05", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "en", "text": "The two words for a group of females are written with the L twice.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["hl:written with two"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-06", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّاتِي", "pause": 0.35, "cues": ["ar:4"]},
 {"id": "c01-tip-07", "scene": "c01-tip", "lang": "ar", "text": "اللَّوَاتِي", "pause": 0.7, "cues": ["ar:5"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-01", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "Now the rule. All of these are fixed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["show"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-02", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "Look at the word for a group of males.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-rule-03", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:0"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-04", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "It ends like a plural. But it never changes.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["hl:never changes"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-05", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "In rafʿ, in naṣb and in jarr, it stays the same.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-rule-06", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِينَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ar:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-07", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "And these two always end in a long ī sound.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["hl:always end in a long ī"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-08", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّذِي", "pause": 0.35, "cues": ["ar:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-rule-09", "scene": "c01-rule", "lang": "ar", "text": "الَّتِي", "pause": 0.8, "cues": ["ar:3"]}
]}
